00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:23.330
TRANSITION
TITLE CARD: THE PSYCHOLOGY OF PACKAGING

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:27.620
Ever wonder why sometimes you can't avoid
the temptation of buying something that you

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:28.810
don't really need?

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:32.730
It's because of the packaging!

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:39.410
Market analysis suggests that consumers, regardless
of what their personality may be, care about

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:40.410
design.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:47.150
42% of shoppers have already admitted that
they base a large number of their purchasing

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:49.660
decisions on design.

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:54.750
If something looks good, consumers feel safer
about the purchase that they've made — and

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:58.390
it's all possible thanks to the psychology
of packaging!

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:05.060
Generally speaking, there are three elements
that affect how people perceive products;

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:09.110
color, shape, and structure.

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:14.810
These three things, no matter how trivial
they may look, can easily influence how people

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:16.580
see your products.

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:22.340
Let's take the common example of what we've
associated with the colors blue and pink!

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:27.310
As kids, we were taught that the color blue
is meant for boys.

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:31.280
Anything that has pink on them is meant for
girls.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:37.020
Besides the similar conditioning we've grown
up with, the colors we see generally affect

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:39.490
our emotional state.

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:44.780
There's a logical reason why major brands
like McDonald's and Coca-Cola love the shade

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:45.780
red.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:50.140
And if you pay enough attention to the other
things that you see in your grocery, you'd

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:57.470
realize that almost every other brand out
there does the same thing but with other colors!

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:05.280
See, besides affecting or eliciting emotions
from consumers, colors are also meant to capture

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:07.630
their attention.

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:11.520
Studies have revealed that the colors red,
pink, yellow, and green are considered to

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:14.580
be the four most eye-catching colors in the
market.

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:20.579
And if you take a quick look at your local
grocery isles, you'll realize just how common

00:04:20.579 --> 00:04:24.169
these four colors are when it comes to packaging.

00:04:24.169 --> 00:04:29.051
The only difference is that each brand uses
its own shade of red or pinks so that its

00:04:29.051 --> 00:04:38.300
products don't magically disappear in a store
filled with green packaging.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:44.169
The rest of what makes packaging design, its
shape, and structure, also has meaning behind

00:04:44.169 --> 00:04:45.169
it!

00:04:45.169 --> 00:04:50.539
These two factors have the ability to become
the most unique identifier of your product.

00:04:50.539 --> 00:04:53.419
Colors don't really say much about your product.

00:04:53.419 --> 00:04:59.610
But if they see your unique packaging after
scanning an entire aisle filled with traditional

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:03.370
packaging, they're probably going to go with
your product!

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:09.750
Additionally, psychology has shown that shapes
have the ability to emotional responses from

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:11.069
consumers.

00:05:11.069 --> 00:05:17.050
Instead of simply letting the shape speak
for their product, brands fill their packaging

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:21.909
with other contextual elements like colors
and texture.

00:05:21.909 --> 00:05:26.580
For example, studies have revealed that consumers
tend to find curved lines more appealing than

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.130
straight ones.

00:05:28.130 --> 00:05:32.410
When people think of beauty, curved lines
are the first thing their brain thinks of

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:37.629
— specifically, the region of the brain
that responds to rewards and emotions!

00:05:37.629 --> 00:05:42.770
If you're planning to make packaging that's
considered different from traditional ones,

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:45.069
keep shape and structure in mind.

00:05:45.069 --> 00:05:49.940
Sure, it'll be fun to make pointed packaging
for milk.

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:56.889
But the thing is, consumers often see sharp
lines as a threat — a response that you

00:05:56.889 --> 00:06:00.919
definitely don't want to elicit from your
fanbase!

00:06:00.919 --> 00:06:06.479
Now, besides harnessing psychology to your
advantage, there's another important element

00:06:06.479 --> 00:06:10.319
that you need to think about when investing
in packaging design!

00:06:10.319 --> 00:06:15.110
TRANSITION
TITLE CARD: THE FUNCTION OF PACKAGING

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:21.099
If you've been in the game for long enough,
then you know how your packaging design can

00:06:21.099 --> 00:06:25.270
easily affect your supply chain and logistics
performance.

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:31.840
For example, oddly-shaped products could make
logistics harder than it normally is.

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:36.999
You need to think about how you're going to
store and handle them — not to mention whether

00:06:36.999 --> 00:06:43.639
your transportation provider can deliver them
safely from one place to another.

00:06:43.639 --> 00:06:48.159
These are some of the important elements of
packaging design that most people don't often

00:06:48.159 --> 00:06:49.159
think about.

00:06:49.159 --> 00:06:55.419
A lot of newcomers think that packaging is
all about the design and the unboxing experience.

00:06:55.419 --> 00:07:02.879
When in reality, logistics and supply can
also affect the overall unboxing experience

00:07:02.879 --> 00:07:05.160
of your consumers.

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:09.949
All of the hard work you've put into creating
pretty packaging will be for nothing if the

00:07:09.949 --> 00:07:16.029
product itself arrives all damaged and broken
to your fanbase!

00:07:16.029 --> 00:07:24.060
Thankfully, professional designers prioritize
the function of their packaging design — alongside

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:26.520
the actual visuals of the product!

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:30.960
When you work with professionals, logistics
and the supply chain will be one of their

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:33.159
top priorities.

00:07:33.159 --> 00:07:37.569
They'll discuss with you how much your budget
should be depending on the packaging you're

00:07:37.569 --> 00:07:39.469
hoping to achieve.

00:07:39.469 --> 00:07:45.110
If you want to go the sustainable route, they'll
explain to you how expensive sustainable packaging

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:46.300
is.

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:51.009
You could ask them for a breakdown of the
pros and cons of traditional as well as sustainable

00:07:51.009 --> 00:07:53.659
packaging.

00:07:53.659 --> 00:07:58.889
When it comes to the actual shape and structure
of your packaging, they'll give you enough

00:07:58.889 --> 00:08:05.830
insight into how each option available in
the market can affect your logistics.

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:12.330
Like we've mentioned earlier, non-traditional
packaging requires non-traditional services.

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:18.940
Additionally, if the material of your packaging
is flimsy, it will require proper handling

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:20.800
during shipment

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:25.569
When all these small details start failing
one after the other, they become a bigger

00:08:25.569 --> 00:08:31.439
problem that's harder to solve — especially
with e-commerce right around the corner.

00:08:31.439 --> 00:08:39.950
Thanks to the recent boost on e-commerce transactions,
customers are constantly searching for faster

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:41.590
and better service.

00:08:41.590 --> 00:08:47.280
They're not just looking for a great unboxing
experience, they want to enjoy fast shipping

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:48.810
too!

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:53.440
And depending on the overall structure of
your packaging, there's no way of ensuring

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:59.120
great quality and proper delivery timing — that's
how important and crucial packaging design

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:02.080
is to your business.

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:07.560
Not only will it allow you to stand out against
your competitors, but it also has the power

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:13.490
to dictate just how fast your logistics and
supply chain operates!

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:20.150
Ultimately, packaging design has the ability
to affect all the crucial parts of your business

00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:22.970
responsible for its success.

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:28.340
If you want to make the most out of your packaging
design, then you need to find a professional

00:09:28.340 --> 00:09:34.160
that understands the crucial role that it
plays to your business!

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:36.180
